Requirements beyond the base project:
- Have 1Password's cli installed (op)

Create the env.xcconfig file by running

```
op inject -i wire-ios/WireUITests/env.xcconfig.tpl -o wire-ios/WireUITests/env.xcconfig
```

Note: the xcconfig cannot handle "//", so take care when adding values


### Run Testservice UI tests (e.g., `*MessagingTests`) locally

#### Prerequisites

- Java 17

#### Install Java 17 (Temurin)

```bash
brew install --cask temurin@17
```

#### Verify Java 17

```bash
/usr/libexec/java_home -v 17
java -version
```

#### Deploy and Start Kalium Testservice

```bash
./scripts/setup-local-testservice.sh
```

#### Verify Testservice is running

Look for the following line in the logs:

```text
✅ Kalium Testservice reachable
```

Once the service is up, run the relevant UI tests locally.

### Mark and run tagged UI tests

Add comment tags directly above a UI test:

```swift
/// [critical]
@MainActor
func testExample_TC_1234() async throws {
    ...
}
```

or UI test class: this will make the whole set of tests for particular scope
```swift
/// [calling]
final class ZCallingTests: WireUITestCase {
    ...
}
```

Tags can be combined inside the same bracketed marker, for example `/// [critical, calling]`.
Class tags apply to every test in that class. Method tags are added to class tags.

Run selected UI tests through fastlane:

```bash
bundle exec fastlane run_uitests tags:critical
bundle exec fastlane run_uitests tags:"calling|core-messenger|collaboration"
bundle exec fastlane run_uitests tags:"critical,calling|core-messenger|collaboration"
bundle exec fastlane run_uitests tags:"!critical"
```

In the fastlane selector, `,` means AND, `|` means OR, and `!` means exclude.
The selector syntax does not use brackets; brackets are only for Swift marker comments. For example,

`tags:"critical,calling|core-messenger|collaboration"`

runs tests that are tagged `critical` and also tagged with at least one of `calling`, `core-messenger`, or `collaboration`.

`tags:"!critical"` runs all UI tests except tests tagged `critical`.

Quote selectors that contain `|` or `!` so the shell does not treat them as special characters.


### Pending teammate onboarding UI tests (TC-12185–TC-12190)

`PendingOnboardingTests` creates a fresh team and a SCIM-managed teammate per test.
The pending teammate is never signed in. The fully onboarded cases sign the teammate
in through Keycloak SSO, then add the team owner's account and run the search flow
as the owner. Setup verifies the teammate's backend contact status before proceeding.

| Case | Coverage |
| --- | --- |
| TC-12185 | Pending teammate is searchable without an onboarding badge. |
| TC-12186 | Pending teammate's profile opens. |
| TC-12187 | Profile displays the setup hint. |
| TC-12188 | Start conversation is disabled; tapping it creates no conversation. |
| TC-12189 | Fully onboarded teammate has a normal profile without the hint. |
| TC-12190 | Start conversation is enabled and creates a conversation. |

Load `env.xcconfig` using the 1Password command above. These tests use the staging
backend and Keycloak configuration already used by `SSOTests`, including
`KEYCLOAK_URL` and `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD`. They do not provision Kalium Testservice
clients; the shared `WireUITestCase` still requires its usual environment settings.

Start with the pending search case, from the repository root:

```bash
bundle exec fastlane ios run_uitests testiny_cases:12185
```

Then run all six:

```bash
bundle exec fastlane ios run_uitests testiny_cases:"12185,12186,12187,12188,12189,12190"
```

TC-12185 passed locally against staging on 2026-10-19 (1 test, 0 failures; about 38 seconds).
The app and UI test target built successfully. TC-12186–TC-12190 have not yet been run.
Resolve setup/network failures before diagnosing the UI assertions. Setup's contact-status
check distinguishes an incorrectly provisioned fixture from a search/profile failure.

Copy review is deferred for TC-12187: it currently checks the implemented text,
"You can communicate with [name] once they are set up." Testiny currently asks for
an "Onboarding pending" heading and different body text. The test does not yet
claim coverage of that heading; align the expectation and product copy after review.
